    {
      "text": "Jubal … was the father of all such as handle the harp and organ, Gen. 4:21. prophets … with a psaltery, and a tabret, and a pipe, and a harp, 1 Sam. 10:5 (1 Chr. 15:16; Ps. 92:1, 3; 108:1–3; 150). cunning player on an harp … shall play with his hand, 1 Sam. 16:16 (Ps. 137:2–4; Isa. 23:16). David and … Israel played before the Lord on all manner of instruments, 2 Sam. 6:5 (2 Kgs. 11:14; Matt. 6:2). people piped with pipes, 1 Kgs. 1:40 (Jer. 48:36; Rev. 18:22). appoint … singers with instruments of musick, psalteries and harps and cymbals, 1 Chr. 15:16. instruments of musick … David the king had made to praise the Lord, 2 Chr. 7:6. They take the timbrel and harp, and rejoice at the sound of the organ, Job 21:12 (Ps. 81:1–3). As well the singers as the players on instruments shall be there, Ps. 87:7. Upon an instrument of ten strings, and upon the psaltery; upon the harp, Ps. 92:3. pomp is brought down to the grave, and the noise of thy viols, Isa. 14:11 (5:12). unto them as a very lovely song of one that … can play well on an instrument, Ezek. 33:32. hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, dulcimer, Dan. 3:5. neither were instruments of musick brought before him, Dan. 6:18 (Amos 6:5).",
